{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,320p' src/vgt/project.py && sed -n '1,340p' tests/test_reascript.py && git show --format=fuller --stat 3ec72dc && gh issue view 7 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json labels,state,body,comments\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,320p' src/vgt/project.py && sed -n '1,340p' tests/test_reascript.py && git show --format=fuller --stat 3ec72dc && gh issue view 7 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json labels,state,body,comments\"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"First implementation task of **Phase 1** ([`docs/GOAL.md`](docs/GOAL.md)). Establishes the analysis stage and the state container everything else writes into. Detectors themselves may be stubs here — later sub-issues fill them in.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- Add a `vgt analyze [project]` CLI stage that resolves the **reference track's source-file path** from the `<project>.vgt` sidecar / project (the reference is already recorded by phase 0's apply).\\n- Extend the sidecar to **`schema_version` 2**: add an `analysis` object (tempo/key/sections/chords sub-objects, initially empty/stubbed) plus provenance (tool + version + settings). Keep all phase 0 fields intact and back-compatible.\\n- **Stage-cache framework:** each analysis stage caches its output keyed on input-hash + settings, so correcting one value doesn't re-run the others.\\n- **Corrections mechanism:** detected values are overridable and overrides survive re-runs (mark corrected fields `human_verified`).\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Analysis runs in the **Python CLI, never inside REAPER** (per the \\\"analysis stays out of the DAW process\\\" requirement).\\n- The `.vgt` sidecar is the contract — reuse it rather than introducing a separate `manifest.json`.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `vgt analyze` runs against `test/Reaper Project` and writes a v2 sidecar with an `analysis` skeleton + provenance.\\n- [ ] Re-running is idempotent; a manual correction to an `analysis` value persists across a re-run.\\n- [ ] Phase 0 apply still round-trips (schema v2 is back-compatible with the existing reader).\\n- [ ] Tests cover schema v2 read/write and the corrections-survive-rerun behavior.\\n\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOTcQqas8AAAABKrBN_w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mrkkucharski\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Fix cycle 1: no reviewer comment was left on the issue/PR to work from (checked issue comments, PR comments, and PR reviews — all empty), so I reviewed the implementation against the acceptance criteria myself.\\n\\nFound and fixed a real bug: `reascript/vgt_initialize.lua`'s `write_settings` unconditionally rewrote the sidecar as `schema_version: 1` on every apply/re-apply, silently deleting any `analysis` block `vgt analyze` had already written. Since the `.vgt` sidecar is meant to be the single shared contract between the ReaScript apply action and the Python analysis CLI, re-applying Phase 0 (e.g. to switch the reference track) was destroying analysis work already done — the reader/writer sides of the contract weren't actually symmetric.\\n\\nFix: the action now reads back any existing `analysis` object before overwriting the sidecar and round-trips it verbatim, only advancing `schema_version` to 2 once analysis exists (a fresh apply with no prior analysis still writes schema 1, so the existing Phase 0 live-verification procedure is unaffected). Verified the Lua brace-balancing extraction logic against nested-object JSON with a standalone interpreter, and confirmed the resulting output is valid JSON in both the with- and without-analysis cases.\\n\\nAll 13 existing tests still pass; this is a REAPER-only code path so it isn't covered by the Python test suite (same limitation as the rest of the Lua apply action).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-18T11:59:01Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mrkkucharski/vgt/issues/7#issuecomment-5011164671\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEnfA\",\"name\":\"status:working\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"1d76db\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEoHw\",\"name\":\"implementer:codex\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"0052cc\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEoaQ\",\"name\":\"reviewer:codex\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"006b75\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEpBQ\",\"name\":\"priority:high\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"d93f0b\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsSEeMw\",\"name\":\"fix-count:2\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"e4e669\"}],\"state\":\"OPEN\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
