{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"command -v lua || true; command -v luac || true; sed -n '1,260p' README.md; git show origin/main:reascript/vgt_initialize.lua | sed -n '1,200p'; rg -n 'analysis|sidecar|schema' README.md docs tests src reascript\"","aggregated_output":"/opt/homebrew/bin/lua\n/opt/homebrew/bin/luac\n# vgt\n\nPhase 0 of virtual guitar teacher: safe REAPER project plumbing. It reads an RPP project from the command line and uses a REAPER ReaScript action to add a small, vgt-owned practice area.\n\n## Install and inspect\n\nWith Python 3.11 and `uv`:\n\n```sh\nuv tool install .\nvgt \"test/Reaper Project/Reaper Project.RPP\"\n```\n\n`vgt [project.rpp]` (or the explicit `vgt inspect [project.rpp]`) accepts an explicit `.RPP` path. Without one it selects the only `.RPP` in the current directory; it refuses to guess if there are zero or multiple projects. It reports the project's sample rate, tempo/time signature, and track names/GUIDs.\n\n## Apply inside REAPER\n\nOpen and save the target project in REAPER 7.x. In **Actions → Show action list → ReaScript: Load**, load [reascript/vgt_initialize.lua](reascript/vgt_initialize.lua), then run it.\n\nThe action is intentionally the mutation path: it uses REAPER's API and never text-edits an RPP. It:\n\n- pops up a menu of the project's own (non-`[vgt]`) tracks and asks which one is the **reference** to mirror;\n- creates a REAPER folder named `[vgt] <reference track name>` (e.g. `[vgt] The Seven Rivers (Full March - 3_00)`) with a `[vgt] Mirror` child;\n- clones only the chosen reference track's file-backed media to the mirror track, without adding sends, changing source tracks, or changing project tempo/sample rate;\n- writes the adjacent `.vgt` sidecar — named after the project, e.g. `Reaper Project.vgt` — with its two created track GUIDs and config recording the reference track;\n- on re-apply, deletes only tracks whose GUID occurs in the sidecar **and** whose current name begins `[vgt]`, then recreates the same area, carrying forward any `analysis` block `vgt analyze` had already written (schema stays version 1 until analysis exists, then becomes version 2).\n\nThe folder/mirror are therefore idempotent and original tracks remain untouched. REAPER-native click-source items have no file to clone, so choosing a click track mirrors nothing. `vgt apply` validates the project path and directs you to this action rather than silently falling back to unsafe RPP editing.\n\nAutomation can skip the menu by setting the `vgt`/`reference_index` ExtState (a 0-based index over the non-`[vgt]` tracks) before running the action; interactive users are always prompted.\n\nUse a copy of any project when experimenting; the included `test/Reaper Project` fixture is read-mostly.\n\nFor a repeatable live-REAPER run against a disposable copy of that fixture, see\n[Phase 0 live verification](docs/phase0-live-verification.md). The verifier\nchecks the saved RPP and sidecar after both the first apply and re-apply.\n\n## Analyze the reference track (Phase 1)\n\n`vgt analyze [project.rpp]` requires a `.vgt` sidecar already written by the\napply action above. It resolves the reference track's source audio file,\nruns the tempo/key/sections/chords detectors, and writes the results back\ninto the sidecar as schema version 2 — never inside REAPER itself.\n\nEach detector's output is cached against a hash of the source audio and the\ndetector's settings, so re-running only recomputes stages whose inputs\nchanged. Any stage can be corrected by hand-editing its `value` in the\nsidecar and setting `human_verified: true`; `vgt analyze` then leaves that\nstage untouched on every later run, regardless of what the audio hash says.\n-- vgt Phase 0 apply action for REAPER 7.x.\n-- Install this file in REAPER's Action List and run it while the target RPP is open.\n-- It is the only writer of REAPER projects: the Python CLI intentionally never edits RPP text.\n\nlocal PREFIX = \"[vgt]\"\nlocal MIRROR_NAME = PREFIX .. \" Mirror\"\n\nlocal function project_path()\n  local _, path = reaper.EnumProjects(-1, \"\")\n  return path\nend\n\nlocal function sidecar_path()\n  -- The sidecar shares the project's name with a .vgt extension (Foo.RPP -> Foo.vgt).\n  local path = project_path()\n  return (path:gsub(\"%.[^./\\\\]*$\", \"\") .. \".vgt\")\nend\n\nlocal function escaped(value)\n  return value:gsub(\"\\\\\", \"\\\\\\\\\"):gsub('\"', '\\\\\"')\nend\n\nlocal function track_name(track)\n  local _, name = reaper.GetTrackName(track, \"\")\n  return name\nend\n\nlocal function starts_with_vgt(track)\n  return track_name(track):sub(1, #PREFIX) == PREFIX\nend\n\n-- Candidate reference tracks are the project's own (non-vgt) tracks, in order.\nlocal function candidate_tracks()\n  local candidates = {}\n  for index = 0, reaper.CountTracks(0) - 1 do\n    local track = reaper.GetTrack(0, index)\n    if not starts_with_vgt(track) then candidates[#candidates + 1] = track end\n  end\n  return candidates\nend\n\n-- Ask which track is the reference to mirror. Automation (e.g. the headless\n-- verifier) can preselect it via the \"vgt\"/\"reference_index\" ExtState, a 0-based\n-- index over candidate_tracks(); interactive users get a popup menu. Returns the\n-- chosen track, or nil if the user dismissed the menu.\nlocal function choose_reference(candidates)\n  if #candidates == 0 then error(\"No non-[vgt] tracks to use as a reference.\") end\n\n  local forced = reaper.GetExtState(\"vgt\", \"reference_index\")\n  if forced ~= \"\" then\n    local index = tonumber(forced)\n    if not index or index < 0 or index >= #candidates then\n      error(\"vgt reference_index ExtState is out of range: \" .. forced)\n    end\n    return candidates[index + 1]\n  end\n\n  local labels = {}\n  for position, track in ipairs(candidates) do\n    -- \"|\" is the menu separator, so it must not appear inside a label.\n    labels[position] = track_name(track):gsub(\"|\", \"/\")\n  end\n  gfx.init(\"vgt: choose the reference track\", 0, 0)\n  gfx.x, gfx.y = gfx.mouse_x, gfx.mouse_y\n  local choice = gfx.showmenu(table.concat(labels, \"|\"))\n  gfx.quit()\n  if choice < 1 then return nil end\n  return candidates[choice]\nend\n\nlocal function read_managed_guids()\n  local file = io.open(sidecar_path(), \"r\")\n  if not file then return {} end\n  local body = file:read(\"*a\")\n  file:close()\n  local guids = {}\n  -- GUIDs are deliberately read only from our schema's managed_track_guids array.\n  local array = body:match('\"managed_track_guids\"%s*:%s*%[(.-)%]') or \"\"\n  for guid in array:gmatch(\"{[%x%-]+}\") do guids[guid] = true end\n  return guids\nend\n\nlocal function remove_previous_managed_tracks()\n  local managed = read_managed_guids()\n  -- A GUID in the sidecar alone is not enough: preserve any track whose current name is not vgt-owned.\n  for index = reaper.CountTracks(0) - 1, 0, -1 do\n    local track = reaper.GetTrack(0, index)\n    if managed[reaper.GetTrackGUID(track)] and starts_with_vgt(track) then\n      reaper.DeleteTrack(track)\n    end\n  end\nend\n\nlocal function find_track_by_guid(guid)\n  for index = 0, reaper.CountTracks(0) - 1 do\n    local track = reaper.GetTrack(0, index)\n    if reaper.GetTrackGUID(track) == guid then return track end\n  end\n  return nil\nend\n\nlocal function copy_file_backed_items(source, destination)\n  for item_index = 0, reaper.CountTrackMediaItems(source) - 1 do\n    local source_item = reaper.GetTrackMediaItem(source, item_index)\n    local source_take = reaper.GetActiveTake(source_item)\n    if source_take then\n      local source_media = reaper.GetMediaItemTake_Source(source_take)\n      -- Lua returns the filename directly (unlike several APIs that return an\n      -- `ok, value` pair). Keeping it in one variable avoids passing nil to\n      -- PCM_Source_CreateFromFile and leaving an empty item behind.\n      local filename = reaper.GetMediaSourceFileName(source_media, \"\")\n      if filename ~= \"\" then\n        local item = reaper.AddMediaItemToTrack(destination)\n        reaper.SetMediaItemInfo_Value(item, \"D_POSITION\", reaper.GetMediaItemInfo_Value(source_item, \"D_POSITION\"))\n        reaper.SetMediaItemInfo_Value(item, \"D_LENGTH\", reaper.GetMediaItemInfo_Value(source_item, \"D_LENGTH\"))\n        local take = reaper.AddTakeToMediaItem(item)\n        reaper.SetMediaItemTake_Source(take, reaper.PCM_Source_CreateFromFile(filename))\n        reaper.SetMediaItemTakeInfo_Value(take, \"D_STARTOFFS\", reaper.GetMediaItemTakeInfo_Value(source_take, \"D_STARTOFFS\"))\n        reaper.SetMediaItemTakeInfo_Value(take, \"D_PLAYRATE\", reaper.GetMediaItemTakeInfo_Value(source_take, \"D_PLAYRATE\"))\n        reaper.SetMediaItemTakeInfo_Value(take, \"D_PITCH\", reaper.GetMediaItemTakeInfo_Value(source_take, \"D_PITCH\"))\n      end\n    end\n  end\nend\n\nlocal function write_settings(folder, mirror, reference)\n  local file, error_message = io.open(sidecar_path(), \"w\")\n  if not file then error(error_message) end\n  file:write(string.format([[{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"managed_track_guids\": [\"%s\", \"%s\"],\n  \"config\": {\"reference_track_name\": \"%s\", \"reference_track_guid\": \"%s\", \"folder_name\": \"%s\", \"mirror_name\": \"%s\"}\n}\n]],\n    reaper.GetTrackGUID(folder), reaper.GetTrackGUID(mirror),\n    escaped(track_name(reference)), reaper.GetTrackGUID(reference),\n    escaped(PREFIX .. \" \" .. track_name(reference)), escaped(MIRROR_NAME)))\n  file:close()\nend\n\nlocal function apply()\n  local path = project_path()\n  if path == \"\" then error(\"Save the REAPER project before running vgt Phase 0.\") end\n\n  -- Choose the reference before mutating anything, so cancelling leaves the project untouched.\n  local reference = choose_reference(candidate_tracks())\n  if not reference then return end\n  local reference_guid = reaper.GetTrackGUID(reference)\n  local folder_name = PREFIX .. \" \" .. track_name(reference)\n\n  reaper.Undo_BeginBlock()\n  reaper.PreventUIRefresh(1)\n  remove_previous_managed_tracks()\n\n  -- Re-resolve the reference by GUID: deleting the previous managed tracks can invalidate the pointer.\n  reference = find_track_by_guid(reference_guid)\n  if not reference then\n    reaper.PreventUIRefresh(-1)\n    error(\"the chosen reference track no longer exists.\")\n  end\n\n  local insert_at = reaper.CountTracks(0)\n  reaper.InsertTrackAtIndex(insert_at, true)\n  local folder = reaper.GetTrack(0, insert_at)\n  reaper.GetSetMediaTrackInfo_String(folder, \"P_NAME\", folder_name, true)\n  reaper.SetMediaTrackInfo_Value(folder, \"I_FOLDERDEPTH\", 1)\n\n  reaper.InsertTrackAtIndex(insert_at + 1, true)\n  local mirror = reaper.GetTrack(0, insert_at + 1)\n  reaper.GetSetMediaTrackInfo_String(mirror, \"P_NAME\", MIRROR_NAME, true)\n  reaper.SetMediaTrackInfo_Value(mirror, \"I_FOLDERDEPTH\", -1)\n\n  -- Clone only the chosen reference track's file-backed media. Every other track stays untouched.\n  copy_file_backed_items(reference, mirror)\n\n  write_settings(folder, mirror, reference)\n  reaper.MarkProjectDirty(0)\n  reaper.UpdateArrange()\n  reaper.PreventUIRefresh(-1)\n  reaper.Undo_EndBlock(\"vgt: prepare managed practice area\", -1)\nend\n\nlocal ok, error_message = xpcall(apply, debug.traceback)\nif not ok then\n  reaper.PreventUIRefresh(-1)\n  reaper.ShowMessageBox(\"vgt Phase 0 failed:\\n\" .. error_message, \"vgt\", 0)\nend\nsrc/vgt/project.py:108:    Used to hand the reference track's audio to the analysis stage, which reads\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:13:local function sidecar_path()\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:14:  -- The sidecar shares the project's name with a .vgt extension (Foo.RPP -> Foo.vgt).\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:71:local function read_sidecar_body()\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:72:  local file = io.open(sidecar_path(), \"r\")\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:80:  local body = read_sidecar_body()\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:83:  -- GUIDs are deliberately read only from our schema's managed_track_guids array.\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:89:-- The Python `vgt analyze` stage (schema v2) adds a top-level \"analysis\"\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:90:-- object to the sidecar. This action is the sole writer of the sidecar's\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:92:-- rather than silently dropping any analysis a user has already run.\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:93:local function read_analysis_block()\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:94:  local body = read_sidecar_body()\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:96:  local key_start = body:find('\"analysis\"%s*:%s*{')\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:114:  -- A GUID in the sidecar alone is not enough: preserve any track whose current name is not vgt-owned.\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:156:  -- Preserve any analysis the Python CLI already wrote (schema v2); a fresh\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:157:  -- sidecar with no prior analysis stays schema v1, matching Phase 0's\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:159:  local analysis = read_analysis_block()\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:160:  local schema_version = analysis and 2 or 1\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:161:  local analysis_field = analysis and ('\\n  \"analysis\": ' .. analysis .. \",\") or \"\"\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:163:  local file, error_message = io.open(sidecar_path(), \"w\")\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:166:  \"schema_version\": %d,%s\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua:171:    schema_version, analysis_field,\nREADME.md:25:- writes the adjacent `.vgt` sidecar — named after the project, e.g. `Reaper Project.vgt` — with its two created track GUIDs and config recording the reference track;\nREADME.md:26:- on re-apply, deletes only tracks whose GUID occurs in the sidecar **and** whose current name begins `[vgt]`, then recreates the same area, carrying forward any `analysis` block `vgt analyze` had already written (schema stays version 1 until analysis exists, then becomes version 2).\nREADME.md:36:checks the saved RPP and sidecar after both the first apply and re-apply.\nREADME.md:40:`vgt analyze [project.rpp]` requires a `.vgt` sidecar already written by the\nREADME.md:43:into the sidecar as schema version 2 — never inside REAPER itself.\nREADME.md:48:sidecar and setting `human_verified: true`; `vgt analyze` then leaves that\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:1:\"\"\"Read/write the `<project>.vgt` sidecar: the shared state contract between\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:2:the Phase 0 ReaScript apply action and the Phase 1+ Python analysis CLI.\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:6:  2 -- Phase 1 adds `analysis`: one entry per detector (tempo/key/sections/chords),\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:34:    \"\"\"The sidecar file is missing or does not contain the data we need.\"\"\"\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:37:def sidecar_path(project_path: str | Path) -> Path:\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:46:def read_sidecar(project_path: str | Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:47:    \"\"\"Read the sidecar for `project_path`, upgrading schema v1 to v2 in memory.\"\"\"\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:48:    path = sidecar_path(project_path)\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:50:        raise SidecarError(f\"No .vgt sidecar found at {path}; run the Phase 0 apply action first.\")\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:56:    \"\"\"Return `data` with all Phase 0 fields intact and a v2 `analysis` block present.\"\"\"\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:58:    upgraded[\"schema_version\"] = SCHEMA_VERSION\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:59:    analysis = dict(upgraded.get(\"analysis\") or {})\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:61:        analysis[stage] = {**_empty_stage(), **(analysis.get(stage) or {})}\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:62:    analysis.setdefault(\"provenance\", {\"tool\": \"vgt\", \"version\": None, \"settings\": {}})\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:63:    upgraded[\"analysis\"] = analysis\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:67:def write_sidecar(project_path: str | Path, data: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\nsrc/vgt/sidecar.py:68:    path = sidecar_path(project_path)\nsrc/vgt/cli.py:10:from .analysis import AnalysisError, analyze\nsrc/vgt/cli.py:22:        \"analyze\", help=\"Detect tempo/key/sections/chords for the reference track and persist them to the .vgt sidecar.\"\nsrc/vgt/cli.py:46:            \"That action uses REAPER's API and creates/updates the adjacent .vgt sidecar \"\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:1:\"\"\"Phase 1 analysis stage: detects tempo/key/sections/chords from the reference\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:2:track's source audio and persists the result into the `.vgt` sidecar.\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:5:\"analysis stays out of the DAW process\" requirement). The detectors below are\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:20:from .sidecar import ANALYSIS_STAGES, SidecarError, read_sidecar, refresh_stage, write_sidecar\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:24:    \"\"\"The project or its sidecar can't be analyzed.\"\"\"\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:65:def reference_source_path(project_path: Path, sidecar: dict[str, Any]) -> Path:\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:66:    config = sidecar.get(\"config\") or {}\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:69:        raise AnalysisError(f\"{project_path}: sidecar has no config.reference_track_guid; run Phase 0 apply first.\")\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:74:    \"\"\"Run (or refresh) analysis for `project` and persist it into the sidecar.\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:82:        sidecar = read_sidecar(project_path)\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:87:        source = reference_source_path(project_path, sidecar)\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:94:    analysis = sidecar[\"analysis\"]\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:97:        analysis[stage] = refresh_stage(\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:98:            analysis[stage],\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:103:    analysis[\"provenance\"] = {\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:110:    write_sidecar(project_path, sidecar)\nsrc/vgt/analysis.py:111:    return sidecar\ndocs/GOAL.md:28:conventions and the `<project>.vgt` sidecar established by the phases before it. \"Done\" for the whole project is\ndocs/GOAL.md:41:- **storing vgt settings next to the REAPER project** — a single sidecar file living alongside the\ndocs/GOAL.md:43:  vgt's own state (schema version, the vgt-managed track GUIDs it created, and any config);\ndocs/GOAL.md:50:### Phase 1 — Reference analysis *(current)*\ndocs/GOAL.md:53:the song, both in the sidecar and as `[vgt]`-owned objects in the project. From the reference audio, detect:\ndocs/GOAL.md:60:- **an analysis stage in the CLI** — heavy analysis runs in the Python CLI, never inside REAPER; the ReaScript\ndocs/GOAL.md:62:- **persisting analysis in the sidecar** — extend the `<project>.vgt` schema (bump `schema_version`) to hold the\ndocs/GOAL.md:64:- **reflecting analysis into the project**, additively and idempotently, as `[vgt]`-owned objects:\ndocs/GOAL.md:72:[phase1-song-prep-plan.md](phase1-song-prep-plan.md) is the longer-range roadmap; phase 1 here is its analysis\ndocs/GOAL.md:86:- **Analysis stays out of the DAW process.** ML/DSP analysis runs in the Python CLI; REAPER only reads the\ndocs/GOAL.md:87:  reference source path and applies results through the API. The DAW never loads heavy analysis dependencies.\ndocs/GOAL.md:88:- **Correctable.** Auto-analysis will sometimes be wrong; every detected value (tempo, key, sections, chords) is\ndocs/GOAL.md:89:  overridable, and corrections survive re-runs of the analysis.\ndocs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:42:└─────────────────────────────────┘        analysis/ manifest.json\ndocs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:68:| Package | write `manifest.json` + human-readable sidecars (`beats.txt`, `chords.lab`, `sections.txt`) | — | — |\ndocs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:82:Auto-analysis *will* be wrong sometimes; the design treats correction as normal operation:\ndocs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:85:- Every analysis stage emits a **checkable artifact**: a click-over-mix render for the beat grid, a printable chord sheet, a section timeline. Trust is earned per song, not assumed.\ndocs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:91:  \"schema_version\": 1,\ndocs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:128:| M0 | Repo skeleton: CLI, config, song-folder layout, manifest schema, stage-cache framework | `vgt prep song.mp3` creates the folder + a stub manifest | S |\ndocs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:156:On the target machine: open an existing REAPER project containing a song item → run `vgt: Analyze selected item` → pipeline completes (LALAL stems + local analysis) → `vgt: Apply results` augments the project per the tables above, non-destructively and idempotently; corrections in `corrections.yaml` survive re-runs; all analysis provenance is in `manifest.json`. Then phase 2 (practice controller: stem muting, loop/tempo management, take recording) builds on the same manifest and the same `[vgt]` track conventions.\ntests/test_analysis.py:7:from vgt.analysis import AnalysisError, analyze\ntests/test_analysis.py:9:from vgt.sidecar import ANALYSIS_STAGES, read_sidecar, upgrade, write_sidecar\ntests/test_analysis.py:23:def _write_v1_sidecar(project: Path) -> Path:\ntests/test_analysis.py:24:    sidecar = project.with_suffix(\".vgt\")\ntests/test_analysis.py:25:    sidecar.write_text(\ntests/test_analysis.py:28:                \"schema_version\": 1,\ntests/test_analysis.py:39:    return sidecar\ntests/test_analysis.py:42:def test_upgrade_keeps_v1_fields_and_adds_v2_analysis_skeleton() -> None:\ntests/test_analysis.py:44:        \"schema_version\": 1,\ntests/test_analysis.py:51:    assert v2[\"schema_version\"] == 2\ntests/test_analysis.py:55:        assert v2[\"analysis\"][stage] == {\ntests/test_analysis.py:61:    assert v2[\"analysis\"][\"provenance\"][\"tool\"] == \"vgt\"\ntests/test_analysis.py:64:def test_analyze_requires_an_existing_sidecar(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\ntests/test_analysis.py:67:    with pytest.raises(AnalysisError, match=\"No .vgt sidecar\"):\ntests/test_analysis.py:71:def test_analyze_writes_v2_sidecar_with_skeleton_and_provenance(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\ntests/test_analysis.py:73:    _write_v1_sidecar(project)\ntests/test_analysis.py:77:    assert result[\"schema_version\"] == 2\ntests/test_analysis.py:80:        assert result[\"analysis\"][stage][\"input_hash\"] is not None\ntests/test_analysis.py:81:        assert result[\"analysis\"][stage][\"human_verified\"] is False\ntests/test_analysis.py:82:    provenance = result[\"analysis\"][\"provenance\"]\ntests/test_analysis.py:86:    on_disk = read_sidecar(project)\ntests/test_analysis.py:92:    _write_v1_sidecar(project)\ntests/test_analysis.py:102:    _write_v1_sidecar(project)\ntests/test_analysis.py:105:    sidecar = read_sidecar(project)\ntests/test_analysis.py:106:    sidecar[\"analysis\"][\"tempo\"] = {\ntests/test_analysis.py:109:        \"input_hash\": sidecar[\"analysis\"][\"tempo\"][\"input_hash\"],\ntests/test_analysis.py:110:        \"settings_hash\": sidecar[\"analysis\"][\"tempo\"][\"settings_hash\"],\ntests/test_analysis.py:112:    write_sidecar(project, sidecar)\ntests/test_analysis.py:116:    assert result[\"analysis\"][\"tempo\"][\"value\"] == {\ntests/test_analysis.py:121:    assert result[\"analysis\"][\"tempo\"][\"human_verified\"] is True\ntests/test_analysis.py:123:    assert result[\"analysis\"][\"key\"][\"human_verified\"] is False\ntests/test_analysis.py:128:    _write_v1_sidecar(project)\ntests/test_analysis.py:133:    assert output[\"schema_version\"] == 2\nsrc/vgt/__init__.py:1:\"\"\"vgt's REAPER project plumbing and reference-track analysis.\"\"\"\ndocs/phase0-live-verification.md:48:saved `.RPP` and its adjacent `.vgt` sidecar (named after the project, e.g.\ndocs/phase0-live-verification.md:53:- the sidecar has schema version 1, exactly two distinct managed GUIDs, and a\ndocs/phase0-live-verification.md:56:- the sidecar GUIDs are exactly the two `[vgt]` tracks: the reference-named\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"I found a concrete edge case in the prior preservation fix: its brace counter treated braces inside JSON strings as structural braces, so a legitimate corrected label/value could corrupt the sidecar on re-apply. I’m making that parser string-aware and adding an executable Lua regression test for nested, escaped JSON content."}}
